{
  "name": "hold_side",
  "note": "(anim-rework S6 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced; M5) Holding a guard, a slow side step to the RIGHT (the left is mirrored by the wiring): a short shuffle (about 12 cm a step) that never crosses the feet, the lead (right) foot lifting low and out, the left closing; the stagger and the low weight of the hold kept, the hips square, the arms on the hold contacts. Not mirrored (8 keys, one step). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in); wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. The arms were solved onto the guard's contacts (his clips posed at the game's hold placement: 0.32 m ahead, 0.1 m to her left, his 1.78 m against her 1.68 m) and written as plain angles: edit these numbers directly. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
